From: Ani <ani@neuronsai.net>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu-base: allow migration blocker to be skipped (QEMU_GPU_ALLOW_MIGRATE=1)

Experimental, for guest-state hibernation on HackberryPi CM5.
Host GPU state (virgl contexts/resources) is NOT saved; after restore the
guest must restart its display server. Only QEMU-side virtio state migrates.

Opt-in via environment variable so stock behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-base.c
@@ -185,7 +185,8 @@
         return false;
     }
 
-    if (virtio_gpu_virgl_enabled(g->conf)) {
+    if (virtio_gpu_virgl_enabled(g->conf) &&
+        !getenv("QEMU_GPU_ALLOW_MIGRATE")) {
         error_setg(&g->migration_blocker, "virgl is not yet migratable");
         if (migrate_add_blocker(&g->migration_blocker, errp) < 0) {
             return false;
